{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And a skin of water.</b> A vessel, and it is possible that it was of skin or of wood, and like it: מְסַפֵחַ חֲמָתְךָ (Habakkuk 2:15). Many will wonder about Abraham: how he banished his son, and also sent a child with his mother empty-handed, and where was his generosity? But the wonder belongs to those who wonder, for Abraham did all that YHWH commanded him. Had he given money to Hagar against Sarah's will, he would not have kept the commandment of HaShem. And behold, in the end, after Sarah's death, he gave gifts to the sons of Ishmael:" "<b>Bread and a skin of water.</b> He gave to Hagar, and placed them on her shoulder, and said to her, take your son, and sent her away. And it is possible that he gave her silver and gold, but Scripture did not specify; and he gave her bread and water sufficient for her until Beersheba, for Abraham was in Gerar. Now she went and did not know the way and lost it, and her son grew ill from lack of water, and after she took him in her lap and saw that his soul was departing from thirst, she cast him aside:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:21.143174765Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}